TDD (T) -> Test driven development testing

job is to test login functionality

1. Write a test case - Pass
2. validate test case by manually testing. - Pass
------ Problem is linking testcase with automation suite ---
3. convert your testcase to automation scripts - Pass
4. Executing it with automation tool - Pass
5. Confirm to team, functionality is working fine - Pass

How will you make sure that test case and automation scripts are for same scenario?
Soln - TestCase has test id, mapping of test id with automation scripts will fix this issue
Next Problem -> You have 6 test steps in a  test case, how will you make sure those steps are covered in automation

This gap of having test steps coverage is filled by BDD (Gherkin language)

The Feature part consists of the test case and the test-steps (feature steps) written inside a feature file
Feature: As a QA, I want to test login functionality so that I can verify the working of the functionality ( Test Functionality)
    Scenario: Test login functionality with valid username and password (TestCase)
        Given: Prerequisite (Pre needed), User navigates to url
        When : Action that you will perform which are user enters the username
        And : user enters the password
        And : user clicks on login button
        Then : Result or the behaviour of application that you observ, user should be able to login / user should be able to go to landing page
        And: Used should be able to see items on the page


